# OptionsAgent — Railway cron schedule (/etc/cron.d format: has the `root` user field).
# Container system timezone is America/New_York (see Dockerfile) so fields fire at
# Eastern clock times, DST handled by the tz database. Every script ALSO self-gates
# internally (ET window + broker market clock), so timing is doubly safe.
#
# Output tees to /proc/1/fd/1 (container stdout) so Railway's log viewer shows cron
# activity in addition to each run's own output.
SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin
TZ=America/New_York

# Daily entry cycle — self-gates to the 10:15-10:27 ET window, once/day (atomic volume lock).
*/5 10 * * 1-5 root /Users/mo/OptionsAgent/cron/entry.sh >> /proc/1/fd/1 2>&1
# Exit sweep — every 20 min on weekdays; self-gates to market hours via the broker clock.
*/20 9-16 * * 1-5 root /Users/mo/OptionsAgent/cron/exits.sh >> /proc/1/fd/1 2>&1
# 0DTE ORB scalper — one fused entry+exit tick every minute during RTH. ISOLATED from the
# seller above; self-gates on OA_SCALP_ENABLED (off by default), the 09:33-15:59 ET window,
# a run-lock, and the broker clock. Inert until the operator sets OA_SCALP_ENABLED=true.
* 9-15 * * 1-5 root /Users/mo/OptionsAgent/cron/scalp.sh >> /proc/1/fd/1 2>&1
# Shared market-data publisher — one SPY/QQQ bar+signals snapshot per minute to the volume,
# for the fleet relay to serve. Self-gates on OA_MARKETDATA_ENABLED (off by default).
* 9-15 * * 1-5 root /Users/mo/OptionsAgent/cron/marketdata.sh >> /proc/1/fd/1 2>&1
# NOTE: a /etc/cron.d file MUST end with a trailing newline (below) or the last line is ignored.
